    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver — here is the decision and the reasoning behind it.\n\nTHE FARE (the ground that decides this case). This trip was sold at a fixed, upfront price. The fare ledger EV-FARE-00524 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd = 12.90, and it records total_charged = 16.10. Nothing on that ledger is separately chargeable on top of the quote: there are no ERP gantries (erp total 0.00), no airport surcharge (airport_surcharge 0.00) and no waiting-time fee (waiting_time_fee 0.00), so the properly_chargeable total is 0.00. Under POL-RD-11(a) the rider is refunded the whole amount by which the charge exceeds the quote plus properly chargeable pass-through lines: 16.10 − 12.90 − 0.00 = SGD 3.20, which is already a multiple of SGD 0.05 and matches the ledger's own computed remedy (pol_rd_11_remedy = 3.20). I therefore rule PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.20 against the SGD 16.10 contested.\n\nTHE RIDER'S TIME COMPLAINT. You said the bill rose because the trip 'took one minute longer'. On an upfront-quoted trip POL-RD-11 fixes the distance and time charges at booking, so extra minutes cannot be charged to you — but the same clause gives no distance-or-time refund, and none is due: the trace EV-GPS-00524 records trace_distance_km 3.37 against a booked optimal of 3.3 km, an excess of only 0.07 km (2.12%), far below POL-RD-01's twin gates of 0.8 km and 20%. Both sides reach that conclusion and I accept it: no deviation exists. So the SGD 3.20 does not come from the driving — it is simply the over-charge of the fixed price.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. You said there was 'some traffic at the last junction'. No traffic advisory for this trip is on file: EV-ADVIS-00524-01 is recorded MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue MISSING_ARTIFACT). Under POL-RD-13 an uncited traffic excuse is tested against the advisory for the trip and nothing else; with no advisory on file the comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. It changes nothing either way, because no deviation was established that would need excusing.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S 'LEAVE THE CHARGE AS IT IS' SUBMISSION. I could not accept the driver's claim that the present payment state should simply stand (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). That argument is right that POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance/time refund is available, and right that there is nothing to add or net under POL-RD-09; but it overlooks POL-RD-11(a). The rider cannot be left paying 16.10 for a trip priced at 12.90. The ledger still shows the charge outstanding and no refund issued, so the SGD 3.20 must be returned. On that point the rider's claims are accepted.\n\nESCALATION AND REFERRALS. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (TRP-00524); the trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (79 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0); the refund is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling; and the missing advisory is a gap in the bundle, not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. POL-RD-06 is not triggered (no material deviation) and, on the driver's profile (deviation_flags_90d 0 across 250 completed_trips_90d), no repeat-deviation pattern exists, so there is no driver-conduct referral. There is no billing-integrity defect under POL-RD-09(4) — no gantry or surcharge line to correct — so no POL-RD-09(4) referral is recorded. No clause produces a referral; the referrals list is empty.\n\nCONFIDENCE. My confidence is 0.95. The deciding fact — that the charge exceeded the fixed quote — is carried by EV-FARE-00524 at full weight 1.0, and no artifact below weight 1.0 carries any part of the decision. The only impaired artifact is the absent advisory, which decides nothing; its absence is noted above."
